<title>HONG KONG: Pearl sells Peak units for HK$918 mln.</title>
<headline>Pearl sells Peak units for HK$918 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pearl Oriental Holdings Ltd said it had sold all the five detached town houses at its Skyhigh redevelopment project in the upscale residential area of the Peak, on Hong Kong Island, for a total HK$918 million.</p>
<p>The company said it had agreed to sell the last 6,000 square feet detached house for HK$198 million, or HK$33,000 per square foot. The price was about 10 percent higher than the HK$30,000 a square foot fetched for the other four houses earlier in March.</p>
<p>Pearl Oriental said the redevelopment cost of the project is about HK$450 million and completion is scheduled for end-1998.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
